Melumzi,

Gerhard Smit here, CTTX in Gqeberha. We engineer owned networks on wind farms=
, reserves and remote sites; we don't sell packages.

You look after the eBOP at Oyster Bay and site management at Tsitsikamma Comm=
unity Wind Farm, so you'll know the real question on a wind farm is resilienc=
e: when the fibre is cut or stolen, does SCADA stay up, can the O&M crews sti=
ll work across the site, and are the perimeter cameras still reporting? A sta=
ndby wireless path that takes over automatically costs far less than a day of=
 lost visibility. We have done this kind of work at Oya Wind Farm and at Esko=
m Medupi.

We've done a desktop terrain study of both sites together, from 30 m satellit=
e elevation data and the mapped positions of all 72 turbines and both substat=
ions. It's attached, one page, no pricing. What it found:

- One standby backbone covers both farms: two coastal-ridge high sites at abo=
ut 180 m, 13.5 km apart with a clear path between them.
- From those two sites, 68 of the 72 turbines are in direct line of sight. Th=
e Oyster Bay substation is 1.4 km from the eastern site and the Tsitsikamma s=
ubstation 8.4 km from the western one, both on clear paths.
- A mapped communications mast gives a 14.1 km candidate uplink into the east=
ern site; its operator isn't tagged in the public data, so that's the first t=
hing to confirm.
- About 50% of the 320 km2 study area is in line of sight of the two sites.

Those positions are desktop candidates until we walk them. What the study say=
s is that the two farms can share one owned standby path rather than each bui=
lding its own.

The next step is a half-day assessment on site: what you have, what fails, wh=
at it costs you when the fibre goes, and what an owned standby path would loo=
k like. R3,500 ex VAT, credited against the build, and the report is yours ei=
ther way. If you can tell me how often the fibre has been cut in the last two=
 years and how long SCADA was blind each time, I'll size the standby path to =
match.

Can I call you for 10 minutes this week?

Gerhard Smit
Director | CTTX Services (Pty) Ltd
gerhard@cttx.co.za | 041 371 1089 | 084 550 3281
www.cttx.co.za

If this isn't relevant to you, reply "no thanks" and I won't follow up.

